<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Scott returns about three weeks before the expedition leaves. The gastroenteritis three weeks ago settled within three days; he held losartan for two days and restarted it once he was eating normally. His home readings over the last week average 124/78 mmHg on losartan 50 mg, and he has had no lightheadedness since the illness. He has not smoked for eighteen weeks and takes varenicline. The sledging rations and the vitamin C tablets are packed. He wants to know what the medical plan is if he or another man falls ill far from the hut, and how he can look after his mind and his sleep through the polar winter and the long journeys. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Home blood pressure</td><td>Seven-day average 124/78 mmHg on losartan</td></tr><tr><td>Recent illness</td><td>Gastroenteritis resolved; losartan held for two days under the sick-day rule</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>No pipe for eighteen weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Mood and sleep</td><td>PHQ-9 2, GAD-7 3; sleeping six to seven hours</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
